        "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{x}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4}}{(-4)}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{4}}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{(-1)^{4}}-\\frac{1}{(-2)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
